{"full":"hf:larryvrh/gpt-image-2-artifact-cleaner","spaceId":"larryvrh/gpt-image-2-artifact-cleaner","name":"GPT Image 2 Artifact Cleaner","source":"huggingface","description":"Remove GPT Image 2's sharpening, specks and scale texture","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"Python","topics":["gradio","image-to-image","artifact-removal","flux","region:us"],"technologies":["Python"],"likes":12,"created":"2026-07-26T16:39:05.000Z","updated":"2026-07-26T16:40:58.000Z","license":"other","runtime":"RUNNING","appUrl":"https://larryvrh-gpt-image-2-artifact-cleaner.hf.space/","demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/larryvrh/gpt-image-2-artifact-cleaner","availability":"available","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T11:13:02.188Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-07T11:13:02.188Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-07T11:13:02.188Z","color":"#3c3250","ink":"#e4d4ff","symbol":"🧼","overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Removes the artifacts GPT Image 2 leaves in its output — excessive sharpening, random bright specks, unnatural edges, and scale-like texture patterns — while leaving the image itself intact.","R is a small residual network (0.48M parameters) that predicts a correction to the image's latent representation. α scales that correction, and it is the only knob.","This is trained specifically for GPT Image 2. The artifacts it targets are particular to that model, not generic AI-image artifacts, so it is unlikely to transfer usefully to output from other generators."],"features":["ZeroGPU: the GPU is attached per request. The first result after an idle period","Quota: visitors get a few minutes of GPU time per day (more with a PRO account).","Up to 16 MP per image. Changing the strength reuses the encoder pass, so it comes","The four strength presets are the ones documented in the repository. Start at 0.5;"],"sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/larryvrh/gpt-image-2-artifact-cleaner/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"872d6bf3f586da75cb658fa8ddf79a09f479a4e1221be6a793